# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Godot 4 build artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Import cache, UID cache, editor layout, shader cache. Entirely regenerated on
# first open, and full of absolute paths from whichever machine created it.
# This is the one entry Godot's own template includes; without it the repo
# fills with noise on every launch.
.godot/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reference material — not ours, not redistributable
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Learning documents used to derive the movement model. They are inputs, not
# part of the project. PLAN.md section 3 records what each one is and section
# 13 records where to get them, so ignoring the binaries loses no information
# and keeps ~1.2 MB of third-party content out of history forever.
*.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Export / build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerate with File > Export. Keep the export_presets.cfg itself tracked.
/build/
/export/
/demo/
*.pck
*.apk
*.aab
*.exe
*.dmg
*.app/
*.zip
*.7z
*.tar.gz

# Only relevant if this is ever ported to C#. Harmless otherwise.
.mono/
mono_crash.*.json
data_*/
*.csproj.old

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS cruft
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
godot.log
*.log

# Personal editor configuration. Share the project, not your keybindings.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.code-workspace

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored — do not add these
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# *.gd / *.tscn / *.tres / *.gdshader   the project itself
# *.uid                               stable resource UIDs, introduced in
#                                     Godot 4.4; Godot expects these to be
#                                     committed so references survive renames
# *.import                            per-asset import settings (icon.svg.import)
# export_presets.cfg                  export configuration
# .gitattributes, project.godot       project configuration
